// Copy this file to Nostalgex/Secrets.xcconfig (gitignored) and fill in your own
// Supabase project. Config.xcconfig includes it when it exists; without it both
// values are empty and enrichment stays off.
//
// xcconfig treats // as the start of a comment, even inside a value, so the URL
// needs an empty $() to split the slashes:
//   SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/abcdefgh.supabase.co
//
// The anon key is public by design. Row level security on media_enrichments is the
// protection (docs/rls-tighten-media-enrichments.sql).
//
// The TMDB key is not plumbed through here on purpose. The app asks the site proxy
// (api/tmdb.js), which holds the key as a Vercel env var. For a dev build that should
// talk to TMDB directly, set TMDB_API_KEY as an environment variable in the Xcode
// scheme instead; a build with a key never touches the proxy.

SUPABASE_URL =
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY =
